---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

// Point of contact for child safety matters, and general questions.
const contact = 'contact@bikes.pizza';
// Reports of content that should not be on the site.
const removals = 'remove.post@bikes.pizza';
const updated = 'September 25, 2026';
---

<Layout
  title="Child safety standards · bikes.pizza"
  description="How bikes.pizza prevents, detects and responds to child sexual abuse and exploitation, and how to report a concern."
>
  <div class="container mx-auto px-6 py-16 max-w-3xl">
    <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-light tracking-wide text-ink">Child safety standards</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-muted text-sm font-light">Last updated {updated}</p>

    <div class="mt-12 space-y-10 text-ink font-light leading-relaxed">
      <section>
        <p>
          bikes.pizza is a place to share photographs of bicycles and pizza,
          operated by Pizza Predator LLC. This page sets out our standards
          against child sexual abuse and exploitation (CSAE), how the service is
          built to keep such material off it, and how to report a concern. It
          applies to the bikes.pizza website and the bikes.pizza apps for iOS and
          Android.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-light text-ink">Our standards</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          We prohibit child sexual abuse material (CSAM) and any content or
          behavior that sexualizes, exploits, grooms, or endangers a minor. This
          includes sexual content involving minors, real or drawn; attempts to
          contact or befriend a minor for a sexual purpose; requests for, or
          sharing of, sexual imagery of minors; sextortion; and the trafficking of
          minors. A member who does any of these things is removed permanently,
          and the matter is reported as described below. Our{' '}
          <a href="/terms" class="text-spice hover:underline">Terms of Use</a>{' '}
          bind every member to these rules.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4">
          bikes.pizza is for people aged 13 and over. It is not directed at
          children, and it does not offer features for them.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-light text-ink">How the service is built to prevent it</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          The subject of bikes.pizza is bicycles and pizza, and the service is
          designed so that images of people, including children, do not appear
          on it at all.
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2 list-disc list-outside pl-6">
          <li>
            <span class="text-ink">Every photo is screened before it is stored.</span>{' '}
            When a member submits a photo, it is sent to Google Cloud Vision.
            SafeSearch detection refuses photos that are likely to contain adult,
            violent, or racy content, and face and person detection refuses any
            photo that shows a person. A refused photo is not stored and does not
            reach anyone.
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="text-ink">A person reviews every photo before it is published.</span>{' '}
            Nothing a member submits is public until an administrator has looked
            at it. A submission that is off topic, shows a person, or breaks the
            rules in any other way is declined.
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="text-ink">Comments and messages are screened.</span>{' '}
            Every comment and every message between members is scored by Google
            Cloud Natural Language's content moderation (categories including
            sexual, toxic, and violent content) and checked against word lists we
            maintain. Text that fails is not posted; text that is borderline is
            held for an administrator.
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="text-ink">Messaging is between members only</span>, is
            text only, and can be turned off entirely in account settings. Any
            member can block another, and a blocked member cannot make contact.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-light text-ink">Reporting a concern</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          Reporting never requires leaving the app. Every post has a{' '}
          <span class="text-ink">Report</span> button at the top of its page,
          every comment and every conversation has a{' '}
          <span class="text-ink">Report</span> action in its menu, and{' '}
          <span class="text-ink">Report a concern</span> in Settings takes a
          report about a post, a member, or anything else. Each report asks
          for a reason, "Child safety concern" among them, and goes straight
          to us. A comment reported by more than one member is hidden
          immediately until an administrator has reviewed it. You can also
          write to{' '}
          <a href={`mailto:${removals}`} class="text-spice hover:underline">{removals}</a>{' '}
          with a link or a description. Child safety reports are handled
          first, ahead of everything else, and we aim to act within 24 hours.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4">
          If a child is in immediate danger, contact your local police or
          emergency services first.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-light text-ink">What we do when we find it</h2>
        <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2 list-disc list-outside pl-6">
          <li>The content is removed from the service at once, and the account that posted it is closed permanently.</li>
          <li>
            Apparent CSAM is reported to the National Center for Missing and
            Exploited Children (NCMEC) through its CyberTipline, and to other
            authorities where the law requires it. We preserve the material and
            the account records for that report, as the law requires, and
            otherwise do not keep or distribute it.
          </li>
          <li>We cooperate with lawful requests from law enforcement.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-light text-ink">Compliance with the law</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          Pizza Predator LLC complies with the child safety laws that apply to
          it, including the reporting obligations of United States federal law
          (18 U.S.C. § 2258A) and the laws of the places where the service is
          offered, and with the child safety policies of the app stores that
          distribute the apps.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-light text-ink">Point of contact</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          Pizza Predator LLC's designated contact for child safety matters,
          including questions from authorities and app stores about these
          standards, is reachable at{' '}
          <a href={`mailto:${contact}`} class="text-spice hover:underline">{contact}</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
